CLASS:: FoaZSynthesis
summary:: FOA Z Synthesis Transform - Synthesizes Height Channel from X/Y with Decorrelation and Ambience
categories:: Libraries>Ambisonic Toolkit>Transform>FOA
related:: Classes/FoaDimension, Classes/FoaEncode, Classes/FoaDecode, Classes/FoaVHAP

DESCRIPTION::
FoaZSynthesis synthesizes the Z (height) component of B-format audio from the horizontal channels (W, X, Y) without requiring a speaker-domain round trip. The W, X, and Y channels pass through unchanged, while Z is either the original input or a synthesized version created from lateral energy.

The synthesis process includes:
- strong::Lateral Energy Extraction:: - Combines X and Y channels, subtracts a small amount of W to avoid centre-bass lift
- strong::Decorrelation:: - Applies short delays to create spatial separation
- strong::VHAP-style Band Splitting:: - Splits the signal at ~1200 Hz, with lows passing direct and mid/high frequencies decorrelated
- strong::B→A Conversion:: - Converts the synthesized Z to A-format (4-channel virtual speaker domain)
- strong::Schroeder-style Ambience:: - Applies lightweight reverb with 4 parallel comb filters and 2 allpass stages per A-channel
- strong::A→B Conversion:: - Converts back to B-format, extracting only the Z component
- strong::Post-processing:: - Applies HPF, soft limiting, high-shelf filtering, and final trim

This transform is particularly useful for:
- Enhancing B-format signals derived from UHJ (where Z was discarded)
- Adding perceptually plausible height to horizontal-only recordings
- Creating spatial ambience and height illusion
- Matching the height characteristics of PHJ-encoded signals

note:: This is a port of the ATK JSFX plugin "FOA Z Synthesis". Default settings (size 2.5, damping 0.2, mix 70%) provide a balanced ambience effect.::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar
Main audio rate processing method.

ARGUMENT:: in
A 4-element array containing B-format components [W, X, Y, Z]. Can be a multi-channel UGen output or array.

ARGUMENT:: heightAmount
Height synthesis amount as a percentage. Range: 0 to 100, default: 30.
Controls the overall level of the synthesized Z component. Higher values create more pronounced height effects. At 0%, no synthesis occurs (only original Z is used if selected).

ARGUMENT:: heightDelay
Decorrelation delay in milliseconds. Range: 0 to 30 ms, default: 7 ms.
The delay applied to decorrelate the mid/high frequency bands. Smaller delays create subtle spatial separation, larger delays can create more pronounced width but may cause combing artifacts.

ARGUMENT:: heightTrim
Height channel output trim in dB. Range: -12.0 to +12.0 dB, default: 0.0.
Final gain adjustment applied to the selected Z output (original or synthesized). Use to match levels between original and synthesized Z, or to adjust overall height channel level.

ARGUMENT:: heightSource
Z source selection. 0=Original, 1=Synthesised, default: 0.
- strong::0 (Original):: - Uses the original Z channel from input
- strong::1 (Synthesised):: - Uses the synthesized Z created from X/Y processing

ARGUMENT:: ambienceSize
Ambience reverb size (RT60) in seconds. Range: 0.1 to 3.0 seconds, default: 2.5.
Controls the reverberation time of the Schroeder-style reverb. Larger values create longer, more spacious ambience. Smaller values create shorter, tighter ambience.

ARGUMENT:: ambienceDampening
Ambience reverb damping factor. Range: 0.0 to 1.0, default: 0.2.
Controls the frequency-dependent damping in the reverb feedback paths. Higher values (closer to 1.0) create darker, more damped reverb. Lower values create brighter, less damped reverb.

ARGUMENT:: ambienceMix
Ambience wet/dry mix as a percentage. Range: 0 to 100, default: 70.
- strong::0%:: - No reverb (dry synthesized Z only)
- strong::100%:: - Full reverb (no dry signal)
- strong::70%:: - Recommended default for balanced ambience

ARGUMENT:: mul
Multiplier for output amplitude. Default: 1.0.

ARGUMENT:: add
Additive offset for output amplitude. Default: 0.0.

returns:: A 4-element array of processed B-format signals [W, X, Y, Z]. W, X, Y are unchanged; Z is either original or synthesized based on heightSource.

discussion::
The synthesis process begins by extracting lateral energy from X and Y channels: (X + Y) * 0.707 - W * 0.25. This creates a decorrelated signal that represents spatial width information.

The signal is then processed through a VHAP-style band split at ~1200 Hz. Low frequencies pass through directly, while mid/high frequencies are decorrelated using a short delay. This preserves bass content while creating spatial separation in the upper frequencies.

The synthesized Z is high-pass filtered at ~1000 Hz before B→A conversion. The A-format conversion uses orientation 2 (FL, FR, BU, BD layout) with Z-only synthesis, creating four A-channels from the single Z component.

Each A-channel is processed through a Schroeder-style reverb consisting of:
- 4 parallel comb filters with different delay lengths (scaled by sample rate)
- 2 cascaded allpass filters for diffusion
- Damping applied to feedback paths
- Wet/dry mix control

The reverb output is then filtered:
- One-pole LPF at ~4.5 kHz to reduce harshness
- Peaking EQ cut at ~3 kHz, Q=1.0, -8 dB to tame mid resonances

After A→B conversion (extracting only the Z component), the synthesized Z is:
- Soft-limited to prevent overload (tanh with k=1.2)
- Gain-reduced by -3 dB
- High-shelf filtered at ~4 kHz, -5 dB to reduce presence

The final Z output is selected between original and synthesized based on heightSource, then trimmed according to heightTrim.

EXAMPLES::

code::
// Basic usage - synthesize Z from horizontal-only input
(
{
    var input = [
        WhiteNoise.ar(0.1),  // W
        SinOsc.ar(440) * 0.1,  // X
        SinOsc.ar(880) * 0.1,  // Y
        0  // No original Z (e.g., from UHJ)
    ];
    
    // Synthesize Z with default settings
    FoaZSynthesis.ar(input, heightAmount: 30, heightSource: 1);
}.play;
)

// Compare original vs synthesized Z
(
{
    var input = [
        WhiteNoise.ar(0.1),
        SinOsc.ar(440) * 0.1,
        SinOsc.ar(880) * 0.1,
        SinOsc.ar(1320) * 0.1  // Original Z
    ];
    
    // Original Z
    var original = FoaZSynthesis.ar(input, heightSource: 0);
    
    // Synthesized Z
    var synthesized = FoaZSynthesis.ar(input, heightAmount: 50, heightSource: 1);
    
    // Switch between them (using a control)
    Select.ar(\compare.kr(0), [original, synthesized]);
}.play;
)

// Adjust ambience parameters
(
{
    var input = [
        WhiteNoise.ar(0.1),
        SinOsc.ar(440) * 0.1,
        SinOsc.ar(880) * 0.1,
        0
    ];
    
    // Large, bright ambience
    FoaZSynthesis.ar(
        input,
        heightAmount: 50,
        heightSource: 1,
        ambienceSize: 3.0,        // Large space
        ambienceDampening: 0.1,   // Bright (low damping)
        ambienceMix: 80           // More reverb
    );
}.play;
)

// Tight, dark ambience
(
{
    var input = [
        WhiteNoise.ar(0.1),
        SinOsc.ar(440) * 0.1,
        SinOsc.ar(880) * 0.1,
        0
    ];
    
    FoaZSynthesis.ar(
        input,
        heightAmount: 40,
        heightSource: 1,
        ambienceSize: 1.0,        // Small space
        ambienceDampening: 0.5,    // Dark (high damping)
        ambienceMix: 60            // Less reverb
    );
}.play;
)

// Integration with Dimension and decoding
(
{
    var input, zSynth, dimension, decoded;
    var decoder;
    
    // Create test B-format input (no Z)
    input = [
        WhiteNoise.ar(0.1),
        SinOsc.ar(440) * 0.1,
        SinOsc.ar(880) * 0.1,
        0
    ];
    
    // Synthesize Z with default ambience
    zSynth = FoaZSynthesis.ar(
        input,
        heightAmount: 30,
        heightSource: 1,
        ambienceSize: 2.5,
        ambienceDampening: 0.2,
        ambienceMix: 70
    );
    
    // Apply Dimension processing
    dimension = FoaDimension.ar(
        zSynth,
        width: 0.0,
        shelvesMode: 2,
        gerzonPresets: 1
    );
    
    // Decode to binaural
    decoder = FoaDecoderKernel.newListen(1053);
    decoded = FoaDecode.ar(dimension, decoder);
    
    decoded;
}.play;
)

// Processing chain: UHJ → Z Synthesis → Dimension → 5.1.2 Decode
(
{
    var stereo, encoded, zSynth, dimension, decoded;
    var decoder;
    
    // Start with stereo source
    stereo = [SinOsc.ar([440, 880]) * 0.1].flatten;
    
    // Encode to B-format using UHJ (no Z)
    encoded = FoaEncode.ar(stereo, FoaEncoderKernel.newUHJ);
    
    // Synthesize Z
    zSynth = FoaZSynthesis.ar(
        encoded,
        heightAmount: 30,
        heightSource: 1
    );
    
    // Apply Dimension
    dimension = FoaDimension.ar(
        zSynth,
        shelvesMode: 1,  // 2D mode for UHJ
        gerzonPresets: 1
    );
    
    // Decode to 5.1.2
    decoder = Foa512Matrix.newFoaDecoder(\equal, 45);
    decoded = FoaDecode.ar(dimension, decoder);
    
    // Output 7 channels (add LFE separately)
    Out.ar(0, decoded);
}.play;
)

// Parameter control with SynthDef
(
SynthDef(\zSynthesisTest, {
    var input, output;
    
    input = [
        WhiteNoise.ar(0.1),
        SinOsc.ar(440) * 0.1,
        SinOsc.ar(880) * 0.1,
        SinOsc.ar(1320) * 0.1
    ];
    
    output = FoaZSynthesis.ar(
        input,
        heightAmount: \heightAmount.kr(30),
        heightDelay: \heightDelay.kr(7),
        heightTrim: \heightTrim.kr(0),
        heightSource: \heightSource.kr(0),
        ambienceSize: \ambienceSize.kr(2.5),
        ambienceDampening: \ambienceDampening.kr(0.2),
        ambienceMix: \ambienceMix.kr(70)
    );
    
    Out.ar(0, output);
}).add;
)

// Control the synth
(
var synth = Synth(\zSynthesisTest);
synth.set(\heightAmount, 50);
synth.set(\heightSource, 1);
synth.set(\ambienceSize, 2.5);
synth.set(\ambienceDampening, 0.2);
synth.set(\ambienceMix, 70);
synth.set(\heightTrim, -1);
)

// A/B comparison: Original Z vs Synthesized Z
(
var input = [
    WhiteNoise.ar(0.1),
    SinOsc.ar(440) * 0.1,
    SinOsc.ar(880) * 0.1,
    SinOsc.ar(1320) * 0.1
];

// Original Z
var original = FoaZSynthesis.ar(input, heightSource: 0);
Out.ar(0, original);  // Left channel

// Synthesized Z
var synthesized = FoaZSynthesis.ar(
    input,
    heightAmount: 50,
    heightSource: 1
);
Out.ar(2, synthesized);  // Right channel (if available)
)
::